    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d779">

                <pb facs="0763" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.5914/44</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Egan to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-08T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 8, 1916, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>207. Referring to my number 203, December 24, 4 p.m. Probably our last
                    opportunity for purchase of Danish West Indies. If Germany is defeated she will
                    need Denmark, if she conquers she will <pb facs="0764" n="598" xml:id="pg598"/>
                    dominate Scandinavia. Danish Government frightened by increasing expenditures,
                    needs money.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Egan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
